usage: ahaecg2mit [-s] -F FREQ -G GAIN -R BITS -U UNITS RECORD.XXX [RECORD.XXX]...
 where RECORD.XXX is the name of the AHA DVD input file to be converted
 ('RECORD' is one of the 4-digit AHA DB record names, and 'XXX' may be either
 'ecg' or 'txt', depending on the version of the AHA DVD.)
 Output files are RECORD.hea (text), RECORD.atr (binary), RECORD.dat (binary).
 Two or more input files may be converted in a single run.
 Use -s to make short-format (35-minute) records from long-format (2.5 hour)
 input files.  When using -s, the second digit in the output record name is
 incremented by 2.
 -F, -G, -R and -U give the sampling frequency (Hz), gain (adu per physical
 unit), ADC resolution (bits) and units of the signals; for the AHA DVD
 files, use -F 250 -G 400 -R 12 -U mV.
